'''Mon Mothma's Senate office''' was located in the [[Imperial Executive Building]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. It was used by [[Chandrilan]] [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] during the late [[Republic Era]] and the [[Imperial Era]].

==Description==
[[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]]'s office in the [[Imperial Executive Building]], in the [[Imperial Plaza]] area on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. The atmosphere of the room suggested serenity and peace with pale [[color]]s, cushioned seats and a view overlooking the clouds.<ref name="Princess of Alderaan" /> The office featured a recessed seating area and was illuminated by natural lighting from a large window facing the Senate Building and skylights.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|mon-mothma-s-senate-office|Mon Mothma's Senate office}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:MonMothmaSenateOffice-WelcomeToTheRebellion.jpg|Thumb|left|300px|Mon Mothma leaving the office so Erskin Semaj can look for listening devices.]]
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Queens Hope Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''Queen's Hope'' to [[22 BBY]].</ref> Mothma spent hours in her office studying the full implications of the emergency powers that [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] had been granted at the start of the [[Clone Wars]].

In [[3 BBY]], [[Apprentice Legislator]], [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of [[Alderaan]], visited Mothma's office with proof she had collected proof of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s cruelty against the planet of [[Chasmeene]].<ref name="Princess of Alderaan" /> During the same year, Mothma met with the Senator [[Dasi Oran]], who represented the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]], in an effort to get support to to challenge the [[Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine's]] extension of the [[Public Order Resentencing Directive]]. Despite Mothma's previous support for the [[Ghorman (people)|Ghorman people]] Oran ultimately decided not to vote against the Emperor's extension fearing a backlash against his people.<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}}</ref>

However during the following year the Empire proceeded with a [[Suppression of Ghorman|campaign]] against the Ghormans, ultimately resulting in the [[Ghorman Massacre]] and the arrest of Senator Oran in [[2 BBY]]. Applaud by the genocide Mothma began work on a speech denouncing the massacre in her office. While she was writing the speech her aid, [[Erskin Semaj]] scanned the room for [[listening device]]s and ultimately finding one planted by the [[Imperial Security Bureau]]. After smashing the device, Mothma left her office to practice her speech outside in the Imeperial Plaza while Semaj continued to scan for more devices. When she returned she had discovered that Semaj had been acting as an operative for [[Luthen Rael]] and rebel associate of Mothma's. After Semaj confirmed that he had finished sweeping for bugs, Mothma confronted him about his betrayal and dismissed him from her service. She later left the office to [[Escape from the Senate|deliver the speech]] and ultimately join the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] as it's public leader.<ref name="Welcome To The Rebellion">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Mon Mothma's Senate office first appeared though unidentified in the [[2017]] novel ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'' by [[Claudia Gray]]. It was later first pictured in the [[Ever Been to Ghorman?|fourth episode]] of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> which aired on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> It was identified as "Mon Mothma's Senate office" in a [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry posted to [[StarWars.com]].

